        "size": 796,
        "text_lines": [
          "---",
          "service: tagged-one",
          "scope: tagged-set",
          "sensitivity: internal",
          "tags: [marketing]",
          "refs: [github:example-org/example-repo#428]",
          "---",
          "",
          "## What it is",
          "An entry carrying ONE of the two tags, so the two tags select DIFFERENT SETS over the wire and a row asking for either cannot pass with the operand ignored. It carries the SAME ref as `tagged-both.md`, which is what makes the cross-filter row reach the reach clause's THIRD state: two entries reference the ref and only one of them carries `internal`, so the `ref-to:` line has to say a FURTHER filter narrows its count. With the ref on one entry only that state is unreachable over the wire.",
          "",
          "## Pointers",
          "- ops skill `manage-gadget` - the same skill, deliberately",
          "",
          "## Nuance / work-history",
          "- 2000-01-02: the lease renewal races the rollout here too.",
